# git ls-files --others --exclude-from=.git/info/exclude
# Lines that start with '#' are comments.
# For a project mostly in C, the following would be a good set of
# exclude patterns (uncomment them if you want to use them):
# *.[oa]
# *~

# What Claude Code's sandbox holds at the top of this folder while a Gamemaker run's commands run (a device or an
# empty file by each name, which can be left behind when a run is killed). They are never part of the work.
/.bash_profile
/.bashrc
/.claude/
/.gitconfig
/.gitmodules
/.idea
/.mcp.json
/.profile
/.ripgreprc
/.vscode
/.zprofile
/.zshrc

# The site has no hidden file of its own but .nojekyll: any other hidden name at its top is Claude Code's or its
# sandbox's, whatever they come to be called, and never part of the site.
/.*
!/.nojekyll
